; Quirk profile for AmigaOS 3.2's stock SYS:Prefs/Time -- see
; manifest/SPEC.md's "Quirk profiles" section: same format/parser as
; an app-shipped manifest, community-authored here since we don't
; control Time Preferences' own source. Every GA_ID and note below was
; discovered live via AmiInspect/amipilot dump against a real running
; window under Copperline (this repo's copperline.local.toml,
; AmigaOS 3.2.3, A1200/AGA, `rtc: none`) -- see
; tests/copperline/stock-app-test.py's own header for the full story.
MANIFEST 1
APP TimePrefs
WINDOW main "Time Preferences"

; quirk: the year string field never accepts typed input, even after
; an explicit click to focus it first -- confirmed live, not assumed.
; This machine profile has no RTC hardware (`rtc: none`); the likely
; explanation is that Time Preferences disables direct date/time entry
; without one, though that's inferred from behavior, not from source.
GADGET year_field main 16

; quirk: buttons are PLACETEXT_IN (baked into rendered imagery,
; GadgetText empty) -- the same, already-documented BUTTON_KIND limit
; fixtures/gadtools-app hits. LABEL= can't address any of them; use
; GA_ID (below) or ROLE=button INDEX=<n> instead.
; quirk: of the three, only "use_button" was confirmed live to close
; the window. Clicking "save_button" (leftmost, conventionally "Save")
; does nothing detectable within a 10s wait -- the window stays open
; and no ENVARC:Sys/time.prefs appears -- consistent with the same
; `rtc: none` theory above but not confirmed by source. "cancel_button"
; (rightmost) was not tested.
GADGET save_button main 2
GADGET use_button main 8
GADGET cancel_button main 9

; quirk: both sliders drag fine via DRAG (no tier-2 form exists for
; DRAG -- GA_ID is the only locator), but neither's resulting position
; is readable back through GETTEXT (only string/integer gadgets expose
; a value=) -- an honest limit of what's observable here, not
; something specific to this app.
GADGET hours_slider main 15
GADGET minutes_slider main 14
